{
  "linkedin": "Heading into the backcountry soon? Practising Leave No Trace principles helps protect our unique New Zealand landscapes for everyone. It comes down to seven simple habits: planning ahead, staying on durable surfaces, packing out all rubbish, leaving what you find, keeping fires small or using a stove, respecting wildlife, and being considerate of other visitors. A great tip for your next tramp is to carry a small rubbish bag in your pack. It weighs nothing and makes a big difference to keeping our trails pristine. Read the full guide here: https://acmeoutdoorgear.example.com/blog/leave-no-trace #LeaveNoTrace #NewZealand #Tramping",
